  "subtitle": "The electronic autoharp that taught you to strum a touch strip",
  "why_scout_cares": "The Omnichord replaced strings with a capacitive touch plate and chord theory with a grid of buttons. You pressed a chord with your left hand and strummed the 'Sonic Strings' touch strip with your right — a genuinely novel bimanual interaction that required learning a new physical skill neither keyboardists nor guitarists already had. It was aimed at people who'd never touched an instrument, and it worked: Bowie played one, Eno slowed one down into ambient beauty, Gorillaz built a hit around its 'Rock 1' preset. Mass-market, musically consequential, and one of the earliest consumer devices where a capacitive touch strip was the primary expressive surface.",
